<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" dir="ltr">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title>OctoStore - Publish your GitHub apps to the Microsoft Store</title>
    <base href="/" />

    <meta name="description" content="Automatically publish your open source GitHub apps to the Microsoft Store">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://early.webawesome.com/webawesome@3.0.0-beta.3/dist/styles/webawesome.css" />
    <script type="module" src="https://early.webawesome.com/webawesome@3.0.0-beta.3/dist/webawesome.loader.js"></script>
    
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: var(--wa-font-sans);
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #f0f8ff 0%, #e6f3ff 25%, #ddeeff 50%, #d4e9ff 75%, #cce4ff 100%);
            min-height: 100vh;
            color: var(--wa-color-neutral-900);
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
        }
        
        .container {
            max-width: 600px;
            padding: 2rem;
            text-align: center;
        }
        
        .logo {
            font-size: 3rem;
            font-weight: 800;
            color: var(--wa-color-primary-600);
            margin-bottom: 1rem;

            img {
                max-width: 200px;
            }
        }
        
        .tagline {
            font-size: 1.25rem;
            color: var(--wa-color-neutral-600);
            margin-bottom: 3rem;
        }
        
        .features {
            margin-top: 4rem;
            text-align: left;
        }
        
        .feature {
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 1rem;
            margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
            padding: 1rem;
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7);
            border-radius: 8px;
        }
        
        .feature-icon {
            width: 48px;
            min-width: 48px;
            height: 48px;
            background: var(--wa-color-primary-100);
            border-radius: 50%;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            color: var(--wa-color-primary-600);
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>
    <div class="container">
        <h1 class="logo"><img src="/icons/octo-store.png" /></h1>

        <p class="tagline">
            Publish your open source apps to the Microsoft Store by adding a single file to your repo.
        </p>
        
        <wa-button href="/auth/login" class="login-btn">
            <wa-icon name="github" slot="start" family="brands"></wa-icon>
            Sign in with GitHub
        </wa-button>
        
        <div class="features">
            <div class="feature">
                <div class="feature-icon">
                    <wa-icon name="zap"></wa-icon>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <strong>Automatic Publishing</strong><br>
                    <span style="color: var(--wa-color-neutral-600);">Just add a ms-store-publish.json file to your repository. We'll automatically publish your app to the Microsoft Store, making your app discoverable to the millions of Microsoft Store users. <a href="https://github.com/JudahGabriel/OctoStore/tree/main?tab=readme-ov-file#how-to-publish-my-app-to-the-microsoft-store" target="_blank">Read more...</a></span>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="feature">
                <div class="feature-icon">
                    <wa-icon name="shield-halved" family="classic"></wa-icon>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <strong>Secure & Trusted</strong><br>
                    <span style="color: var(--wa-color-neutral-600);">Microsoft manages the publishing of your app in the Store under the <strong>Open Source Apps on GitHub</strong> publisher.</span>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="feature">
                <div class="feature-icon">
                    <wa-icon name="eye"></wa-icon>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <strong>Track Status</strong><br>
                    <span style="color: var(--wa-color-neutral-600);">Monitor all your app submissions to the Microsoft Store in one dashboard. </span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="feature">
                <div class="feature-icon">
                    <wa-icon name="windows" family="brands"></wa-icon>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <strong>Native and Web</strong><br>
                    <span style="color: var(--wa-color-neutral-600);">It doesn't matter if your app is Win32, PWA, UWP, MSIX, you name it. OctoStore can publish your app to the Store.</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>